d1-3B for LiteRT

The LiteRT graphs (*.tflite) and the tables (tables/) in this repository are converted from LiquidAI/d1-3B, revision
da1fe36a861f24690f27f622dca1d8688503d113 (https://huggingface.co/LiquidAI/d1-3B), by Liquid AI. d1-3B is post-trained
from LiquidAI/LFM2.5-VL-3B (https://huggingface.co/LiquidAI/LFM2.5-VL-3B). Both are licensed under the LFM Open License
v1.0; LICENSE is a copy of the d1-3B repository's LICENSE file. Every graph and table is derived from that repository's
model.safetensors: the changes are listed under "Changes from the original work" in README.md and in REPRODUCE.md.
tokenizer/tokenizer.json is that repository's file, unchanged.

The Python host (host/) ports the request handling of the d1-3B repository's code (prompt.py, runner.py and api.py at
the revision above, LFM Open License v1.0) and the picture preprocessing of transformers 5.14.1 (Lfm2VlProcessor,
Lfm2VlImageProcessor, Siglip2VisionEmbeddings and Lfm2VlMultiModalProjector, Apache License 2.0), including PyTorch's
uint8 antialiased bicubic resize and float32 antialiased bilinear interpolation (BSD 3-Clause License), as numpy code.
The conversion scripts (conversion/) run the d1-3B repository's model code with transformers 5.14.1, litert-torch,
ai-edge-quantizer and LiteRT (ai-edge-litert), each licensed under the Apache License 2.0; their quantization recipes and
attention forms follow the conversion scripts of litert-community/Kev-0.8B-LiteRT (Apache License 2.0).

fixtures/ lists 382 test requests (fixtures/requests_public.json). 161 are included with their text: 144 are SemIf
authored144 records (github.com/TheoLeeCJ/SemIf, commit ca3ba65f), Copyright (c) 2026 TheoLeeCJ, licensed under the
MIT License (fixtures/LICENSE-SemIf-MIT.txt); 2 are the example requests of the d1-3B model card; 15 were written for
these conversions. 221 are listed by reference only (file, tag, line and SHA-256): 220 records of the transfer-v4
development file of github.com/jaredpalmer/kev at tag kev-1.0 (Apache License 2.0) and one control derived from one of
them. Their text comes from public datasets under their own licenses and is not included; fixtures/rebuild_requests.py
restores it from that file. Of the four control requests (fixtures/red_arms_public.json), the two derived from SemIf
records are included with their text and the two derived from transfer-v4 records are listed as a rule over their base
record. fixtures/reference_probs.json holds the float32 probabilities of the d1-3B code for every test question it answers,
without text.
The photo of the card's picture example (COCO val2017 000000039769.jpg) is not included: the fixture and the example
give its URL and SHA-256.

